<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22674" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-curvus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>bent</i>, <i>bowed</i>, <i>crooked</i>, <i>curved</i> (opp. recurvus, pandus; class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incurvus, tremulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 2, 3, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incurvi umeris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 52, 114, § 274</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lituus, id est incurvum, et leviter a summo
					inflexum bacillum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 17, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statua Stesichori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 2, 35, § 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aratrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 494</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 12, 41, § 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 534</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 376</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
